▎ Auto mode is now Claude Code's default permission mode.
▎ Auto mode lets Claude handle permission prompts automatically.
▎ Claude checks each tool call for risky actions and prompt
▎ injection before executing, runs the ones it assesses as
▎ lower-risk, and blocks the rest.
▎ https://code.claude.com/docs/en/permission-modes

❯ This is a UI test in a scratch folder. Use the
  AskUserQuestion tool once, with exactly 3 questions in the
  same call: (1) single-select 'Which color?' with options Red
  (mark it Recommended), Green, Blue; (2) single-select 'Which
  size?' with options Small, Medium, Large and NO recommended
  option; (3) multi-select 'Which toppings?' with options
  Cheese, Olives, Basil. After I answer, reply with one line
  summarizing my answers and stop.
